From 32ebec90ad630890b6df97ee6eb944add635c7d3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: reaper <theunbounddeveloper@outlook.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 18:42:58 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] libdisk: a refused SMB login reaches the system log (102.8
 line)

Samba 4 logs authentication in its auth_audit class, a refusal at level 2 and a success at 3;
smb.conf set log level 0, so a wrong password left no line anywhere (field report). For Samba 4:
log level = 0 auth_audit:2 and logging = syslog@2 file. Each refused login is in the system log
with the user, the client address and the reason; successful logins and everything else stay as
before.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 release/src/router/libdisk/write_smb_conf.c | 9 +++++++++
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+)

diff --git a/release/src/router/libdisk/write_smb_conf.c b/release/src/router/libdisk/write_smb_conf.c
index 96dd3da941a..5c2fb3761b9 100644
--- a/release/src/router/libdisk/write_smb_conf.c
+++ b/release/src/router/libdisk/write_smb_conf.c
@@ -406,7 +406,16 @@ int main(int argc, char *argv[])
 	fprintf(fp, "printing = bsd\n");
 	fprintf(fp, "printcap name = /dev/null\n");
 	fprintf(fp, "log file = %s\n", SAMBA_LOG);
+#if defined(RTCONFIG_SAMBA4)
+	/* reaper 2026-11-03 (owner: a wrong SMB password left no trace): Samba logs authentication in the auth_audit
+	 * class, a refusal at level 2 and a success at 3 (auth/auth_log.c). Raise that class to 2 and send levels
+	 * 0..2 to syslog: every refused login is in the system log with the user, the client address and the reason;
+	 * successful logins and everything else stay at level 0 as before. `logging` replaces the deprecated `syslog`. */
+	fprintf(fp, "log level = 0 auth_audit:2\n");
+	fprintf(fp, "logging = syslog@2 file\n");
+#else
 	fprintf(fp, "log level = 0\n");
+#endif
 	fprintf(fp, "max log size = 5\n");
 
 	// account mode
